build: 2026-06-26 v10.76.30 (Prism look — sound refracted into natural daylight)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Builds on 10.76.29. Adds the PRISM look (#16) — the rainbow/prism aspect the
  founder asked for, as natural light. A new, opt-in look (alongside Donuts/Rings/
  Chladni/Plasma/Water) that refracts the sounding tone across the frame like white
  light through glass: horizontal position fans the tone's neighbourhood across the
  full Cousto colour wheel — a rainbow centred on what you hear. Coherence narrows it
  to a purer spectrum. Rendered through the app's warm-daylight pipeline, so it reads
  as natural light, not neon.
  Chosen the lambda way: a SEPARATE look, so the existing default looks are untouched
  (no Unstimmigkeit). Selectable in the quick strip, the blend list, and the new
  visuals menu (its own "Prism" category). Flash-safe (slow pulse only; colour fixed
  per location). Shader compiles at runtime with a clear-colour fallback → cannot
  affect launch. Reviewed GO (dsp/shader: ordering, types, numerics, flash-safety).
  Test: 10.76.30 launches? Visual → "Looks & Farboktave…" → Prism (or the strip).
  Play a note → a warm rainbow fans across the frame, centred on the tone; raise
  coherence → the spectrum tightens. Try Mix with Water/Plasma for a blended look.
